ype": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information on instructions about basic activities and safety at work.  ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals for Ability", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the modal<span class=\"strong\"> can </span>to talk about ability -- what you are able to do or not able to do. The negative form is <span class=\"strong\">can't</span>. They go before a verb in the base form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Can you explain that? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I can help you. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I can't do that. I'm nervous!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Responding to Good News", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are different ways to respond to good news.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<li> Congratulations! <li> That's great/fantastic/wonderful! <li> What great/fantastic/wonderful news! <li> That's great/fantastic/wonderful news! <li> I'm glad to hear that!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: I have a new job!<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Tammy:</span> That's great!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "upcoming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening soon", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have an interview this upcoming week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about an interview.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nervous ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "worried; frightened about something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm really nervous about this interview!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make a good impression ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have someone remember you in a positive way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to make a good impression at a job interview. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "confidence ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the idea that you can do things well ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have complete confidence in you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to project an image ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to represent yourself in a specific way  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to project an image of confidence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "candidate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who applies for a job ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can act like the perfect candidate for the job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "advice ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an opinion you give someone about what they should do ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you have any advice for me?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Your friend tells you good news. Write a dialogue. (6-8 lines)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You respond to the good news.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I give good news to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I respond to good news.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use words to describe how I feel.", "type": "text"}]}]}